@*
 * FILE ROLE: Automatically executed before every view in Views/ and its
 *            subfolders.  Sets the default Layout for all content views.
 * SECTIONS IN THIS FILE:
 *   1. _ViewStart.cshtml execution model
 *   2. Per-folder override pattern
 *@

@*
 * SECTION 1: _ViewStart.cshtml EXECUTION MODEL
 *
 * ASP.NET Core's Razor engine runs _ViewStart.cshtml automatically before
 * rendering any content view in the same folder or any sub-folder.
 *
 * Key rules:
 *   - Runs BEFORE the content view (.cshtml) is processed
 *   - Assigns Layout, ViewData, or any shared Razor state
 *   - A content view can OVERRIDE what _ViewStart set:
 *       @{ Layout = null; }                                  opt out
 *       @{ Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_AlternateLayout.cshtml"; }  use different layout
 *   - The layout name "_Layout" is resolved by the Razor view engine using
 *     the standard search paths defined by RazorViewEngineOptions.ViewLocationFormats.
 *     It resolves to Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml.
 *
 * SECTION 2: PER-FOLDER _ViewStart OVERRIDE
 *
 * Place a _ViewStart.cshtml inside a subfolder to change the Layout for only
 * that area.  The subfolder file is executed INSTEAD of the parent — Razor
 * does NOT chain or merge them; the most specific one wins.
 *
 * Example — admin area:
 *   Views/_ViewStart.cshtml           →  Layout = "_Layout"        (all views)
 *   Views/Admin/_ViewStart.cshtml     →  Layout = "_AdminLayout"   (only /Admin/*)
 *
 * This hierarchy is the same mechanism used by Areas (→ 10. Areas) where
 * each Area folder carries its own _ViewStart.cshtml.
 *@
@{
    Layout = "_Layout";     // resolved to Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml
}
